items.checkbox:
In docs/user_guide/loading-iris-level-2-raster-and-sji-data.rst, document existing workflows that need no code:
- the observation-list columns and grouping;
- tick + 'Load selected' versus File→Open;
- previewing an SJI: auto-opened Image viewer, slice-widget playback, contrast/stretch;
- saving the current view from the toolbar Save menu as PNG/JPEG/PDF/PS/EPS/SVG;
- IRIS mask overlays: Histogram x-range or 'Create faceted subsets' on the '<label> mask' component, or 'Import subset mask(s)' for an external integer FITS mask cube of the same shape;
- layer and Preferences styling.

Reword the plan:1012-1013 non-goal ('No full IDL widget/UI clone, OBS XML resolver, detector mosaic reader, PostScript workflow or generic annotation/plugin framework') so that it excludes the IDL PS-device workflow, not .ps/.eps export.

Port the WP8 filter and threaded scan. This refines plan:953 ('Add one case-insensitive text filter for STARTOBS/OBSID/description') and plan:957-962 ('Run header scanning through the existing Worker with a cooperative stop predicate ... Initialize the busy bar with a valid value'). Run scan_directory in glue's existing Worker, and poll the stop predicate while the tree is enumerated as well (collect paths in a loop, then sort) so that Stop, Cancel and close never freeze the GUI. Also:
- disable Load while a scan runs;
- mark observations truncated by a Stop as '(partial scan)';
- show 'Scan stopped' only if the worker was still running;
- repair the progress value after busy mode, as the refreshed prototype does;
- let the filter also match child window/SJI/AIA names, and show a count of hidden ticked items.

Bring the deferred pre-scan search into scope, replacing plan:1028-1029 ('Browser date widgets, pre-scan time-range search and persistent filter text are deferred') and the 'extra filename-preset system' exclusion at plan:970-971. Add keyword-only start/stop/glob/date_tree arguments to scan_directory that prune before any header read:
- skip files whose _key_from_name stamp lies outside the window;
- apply an fnmatch glob (default '*');
- in date-tree mode, descend only into YYYY/MM/DD directories inside the window;
- optionally skip header reads for further rasters of an observation already keyed by filename.

Expose a Start/Stop UTC window in the browser with 'Last 5 days' and 'Up until now' presets and an ignore-times toggle. Add find_observation_files(time, root, sji=False, nearest=False) over scan_directory, returning the covering observation's raster repeats or SJIs (parity with iris_find_file).

Build remote discovery on sunpy[net], which glue-solar already requires, rather than a new client. Add a menubar_plugin 'IRIS: search online…' that:
1. calls Fido.search(a.Time(...), a.Instrument('IRIS')); verified 2026-09-27: VSO returns per-observation Level-2 records from provider LMSAL, including SJI per channel, deconvolved variants and the raster archive;
2. filters by OBSID from the returned fileid;
3. fetches the ticked rows with Fido.fetch in the existing Worker into a chosen folder;
4. opens QtIRISImporter on that folder, which already extracts raster .tar.gz files.

Do not rebuild the LMSAL search page (FOV, cadence and target filters, AIA footprints, www preview movies); link to it from the dialog.

items.done_when:
Mocked-network tests:
- search results are grouped by observation;
- the OBSID filter works;
- Cancel does no network work;
- a fetch error leaves the folder and the data collection unchanged.

An opt-in network test (skipped by default) downloads the roughly 39 MB SJI_1400 record of 2021-04-29 observation 3660259102, and the browser lists it under that observation. Two things are still unverified: whether downloads work, and the LMSAL page URL (iris.lmsal.com returned 403 to WebFetch).

items.checkbox:
Schedule the 'later solar extension' at plan:493 ('sequence selection, stable scaling/annotations and export/encoding with cancellation') and plan:1017-1018 as a viewer_tool 'solar:save_sequence', appended to the Image viewer's existing 'save' subtools next to mpl:save. The tool asks for a slice axis (time, scan or exposure; wavelength for a line scan) and an index range, then steps that viewer's slider so that the M0 time sync moves the other panels. Output options:
- one PNG/JPEG per frame via figure.savefig (viewer only);
- one PNG/JPEG per frame via GlueApplication.screenshot() (whole window, e.g. including the spectrum);
- a movie via matplotlib.animation: FFMpegWriter (MP4) when ffmpeg is on PATH, otherwise PillowWriter (GIF).

Freeze display limits for the run, poll a QProgressDialog Cancel between frames, and restore the original slice. No new dependency is needed; open glue #2128 (hide axes) is optional for frames without axes.

Extend solar:save_sequence and single-frame saves with export options:
- a text artist in the axes with the frame's UTC time, read from the dataset's Time component at the current slice (the value solar:frame_time already shows, glue_solar/tools.py:22-66);
- an arcsec scale bar of chosen length (matplotlib mpl_toolkits.axes_grid1 AnchoredSizeBar, sized from the viewer's WCS pixel scale);
- optional frame numbering;
- a default file name built from OBSID, STARTOBS, label and axis range, pre-filled and editable.

Subsets and markers are already exported as displayed.

Register a glue-solar data_exporter (glue.config.data_exporter) 'FITS (IRIS WCS + Time)' for datasets whose coords are _GlueWCS. It is needed because stock gridded_fits.py:52@1.27.0 writes a header only for astropy WCS and drops the non-numerical Time, and HDF5 export raises on datetime64. For each dataset it writes:
- each numerical component as an ImageHDU with the unwrapped raw WCS header (D3 display units in CUNITn);
- a WCS-TABLE HDU for -TAB axes, reusing WP3's -TAB record;
- the mask;
- Time as MJD with TIMESYS=UTC.

This covers WP2 moment maps, WP6 fit maps, the WP5 Doppler image and sliced raster maps. Refuse gWCS-only SJI/AIA cubes with a message that names the source file.

Extend the WP12 path tool:
- keep several saved traces visible on the image with core's MultiTracePathSlicerMixin (glue/plugins/tools/path_slicer/multi_trace.py@1.27.0), each with its own line style and an optional 'show only at wavelength index w' setting;
- reopen a trace's PathSlicedData in a new Image viewer;
- add a TANAT-style two-click slope readout on distance–time diagrams: projected speed in km/s (path offset in arcsec × DSUN_OBS, Δt from the Time component) and a three-point parabolic acceleration, appended with an ID and flag to an ECSV table.
